<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Ruins, handed a frame.

  Vanilla's machine kit - the racks, the monitor banks, the lamps - is all
  scenery: it is dropped onto maps by the generator and no player ever builds
  it. A def gets a blueprint and a frame if and only if BuildableDef
  BuildableByPlayer is literally "designationCategory != null", which is the
  only condition separating Worksite from a server rack. The category
  itself never shows: the Architect button is stripped and the two roads into
  its menu are gated on the same Visible the bar reads.

  They are the right shape for this map in a way nothing player-buildable is.
  They cost nothing and want no stuff, so a frame is ready the tick it is
  placed; they ask for no construction skill, so every agent that lands can
  raise one; and they arrive already ruined, which is what a machine told
  nothing about what for builds when it copies the world it came out of.

  Wrapped, like every operation of ours that rewrites a def the base game
  shipped: outside a SlopWorld profile it is not applied at all - the Architect
  menu that stays stripped here is a menu somebody else still uses. See
  Source/SlopWorld/ModProfile.cs.
-->
<Patch>
  <Operation Class="SlopWorld.PatchOperationInProfile">
    <operations>
      <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
        <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[
          defName='AncientLamp' or
          defName='AncientLamppost' or
          defName='AncientSystemRack' or
          defName='AncientDisplayBank' or
          defName='AncientLockerBank' or
          defName='AncientGenerator' or
          defName='AncientMachine']</xpath>
        <value>
          <designationCategory>Misc</designationCategory>
        </value>
      </li>

      <!--
        The ancient machine is Impassable and only half-filling, and ThingDef
        ConfigErrors calls that combination an error the moment a def becomes
        player-buildable - a wall you can shoot over. Nothing on this map shoots.
      -->
      <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
        <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName='AncientMachine']</xpath>
        <value>
          <disableImpassableShotOverConfigError>true</disableImpassableShotOverConfigError>
        </value>
      </li>
    </operations>
  </Operation>
</Patch>
